Final Fantasy type-0 is one of the best  entries in the franchise to come out in  recent years the story is set in  Orient's a world torn apart by war you  get a group of gifted teenagers class 0  through campaigns against enemy nations  while unraveling the secrets of your  existence and the mysterious powers  behind the war the story of class 0 is a  little convoluted but with 14  drastically different personalities to  contend with conversations among them  are never boring but the real heart of  the story is REM and máquinas romance  these two try to balance fighting their  own demons as well as beside class 0  struggling to protect each other and do  what they think is right the main  narrative however gets convoluted very  quickly concepts and ideas are  introduced briefly never fully explained  and then thrown into high importance  later in the game things get a little  weird a little too quickly without much  cushioning but the way the game handles  relationships through the lens of war is  heartwarming type zeroes combat however  is marvelous you're fourteen playable  characters have four moves each  available to them all of which can be  customized you have three characters on  the battlefield at any time but can only  directly control one the other two are  guided by some very effective smart AI  you're never left swinging on your own  your skirmishes feel like a cohesive  team rather than a single hero  accompanied by unnecessary deadweight  you can also swap between your three  characters on the fly switching up who  you control directly typically you take  on dozens of giant mechs and angry  soldiers and story missions but when  crossing the overworld random encounters  crop up these entail quickly mowing down  a group of enemies for experience points  if there are other enemies nearby they  detect your presence and the game gives  you the option to immediately fight them  or retreat this is an excellent way to  amass quick experience points and  materials but the repetition is a rarely  tedious small touches like the combat  swirl wind speed and the option to  repeatedly fight the same encounter mean  you don't have to waste time hoping from  our foes to appear in story missions you  run through a maze of connecting rooms  destroying enemies mercifully type-0  adds a handful of checkpoints to each  level allowing you to save frequently  some battles add other combat elements  like airstrike support and bosses that  only take damage from well-timed  critical hits missions constantly change  up their layout and goals giving rise to  a vast number of combat situations and  strategy  not only our missions varied but so are  the combat systems of each class zero  member swords size flying cards a magic  flute it's great testing them all out  and customizing their attack retinues  all Toltecs zero does combat and  customization better than many of its  fellow current role-playing games  type zero looks good but it's an uneven  visual experience due to the  inconsistency of its high-definition  paint job the main characters look great  but characters who are not part of class  zero or are not important to the  storyline don't benefit from the same  care and attention Final Fantasy type-0  is about the fluid and frantic action  the overarching story is a little messy  but it vividly addresses the ugly side  of war the blood the gore and the  sadness that lingers even after you  forget what you've been fighting for  it's a worthwhile investment for the  battle system alone and the world of  Orient's feels truly alive
 

